            <ArticleTitle>What workup should we require for a patient who has had one TIA and demonstrates 80% carotid stenosis?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>305-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The workup that I would recommend of a patient with a single TIA and an 80% carotid stenosis would include carotid ultrasound combined with MRA. If these studies correlated, then I would proceed with carotid endarterectomy after medicine or cardiology consultation and workup for coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
